Implements P99-style level-difference XP penalties so players are pushed toward tougher content as they level up. Green-con enemies yield zero XP; red-con enemies give a 25% bonus. Loot is unaffected.

## Con color table

| Color | Diff | XP Multiplier |
|---|---|---|
| 🔴 Red | +4 or more | ×1.25 |
| 🟡 Yellow | +1 to +3 | ×1.0 |
| ⚪ White | 0 | ×1.0 |
| 🔵 Blue | −1 / −2 / −3 | ×0.8 / ×0.65 / ×0.5 |
| 🩵 Light Blue | −4 to −6 | ×0.25 |
| 🟢 Green | −7 or below | ×0 |

## Changes

- **`js/combat.js`** — New `getConColor(partyLevel, enemyLevel)` returns `{ color, label, multiplier }`. `handleEnemyDeath()` now computes XP as `floor(enemy.xp × zoneModifier × conMultiplier)` and logs the con label. Fallback of `1` added to `Math.max(…living levels…, 1)` guards against a full-wipe edge case.

```js
const highestLevel = Math.max(...GameState.party.filter(m => m.isAlive).map(m => m.level), 1);
const { multiplier: conMultiplier, label: conLabel } = getConColor(highestLevel, enemy.level);
const xpGain = Math.floor(enemy.xp * zoneXpModifier * conMultiplier);
```

- **`js/ui.js`** — `updateEnemyDisplay()` prefixes the enemy name with a `con-dot` span. `renderEnemySelector()` injects the dot into each enemy button's level line.

- **`js/tooltips.js`** — `getEnemyTooltipHTML()` shows a **Con:** row with the colored label and reports effective XP alongside the base value in muted text.

- **`css/style.css`** — `.con-dot.con-{red|yellow|white|blue|lightblue|green}` color classes.

- **`css/tooltips.css`** — `.tt-muted` for secondary tooltip text.

`getConColor` is defined in `combat.js`, which is loaded before `ui.js` and `tooltips.js` in `index.html`, so no load-order changes are needed.

