## Feature: Con-Color XP Scaling (EverQuest-style level-difference XP penalty)

Add an EverQuest/P99-style "con color" system that reduces (or zeroes out) XP when killing enemies that are much lower level than the party. This is the classic mechanism that forces players to progress to tougher content.

---

## How it works

In EQ/P99, each enemy is "conned" (considered) relative to the **highest level living party member**. The con color determines the XP modifier applied to the enemy's base XP:

| Con Color | Level Difference (enemy vs. highest party member) | XP Multiplier |
|---|---|---|
| 🔴 Red | Enemy is 4+ levels **above** | ×1.25 (bonus) |
| 🟡 Yellow | Enemy is 1–3 levels **above** | ×1.0 |
| ⚪ White | Even level (±0) | ×1.0 |
| 🔵 Blue | 1–3 levels **below** | ×0.8 → ×0.5 (scaled) |
| 🩵 Light Blue | 4–6 levels **below** | ×0.25 |
| 🟢 Green | 7+ levels **below** | ×0 (no XP) |

Exact scaling for blue con (1–3 levels below):
- 1 level below → ×0.8
- 2 levels below → ×0.65
- 3 levels below → ×0.5

---

